# Build artefacts, except the one wheel that has to ship.
#
# Same failure as api/vendor/: this directory was `*`, requirements.txt installs
# `../../vendor/agentfox-0.3.0-py3-none-any.whl` by name, and that file was never in
# the repository — so every Vercel build of this demo failed on a missing local path
# while the wheel sat on whichever laptop last ran `uv build`.
#
# Negating the one filename means a rebuild shows up in `git status` like any other
# change. See api/vendor/.gitignore, which carries the same note.
*
!.gitignore
# Any version, not a pinned filename: bumping the version changes the wheel's
# NAME, so a pinned negation silently stops tracking the new wheel while the
# old one stays committed — the deploy then keeps installing the previous
# release with nothing failing anywhere. Found on the 0.3.0 -> 0.3.1 bump.
!agentfox-*.whl
